## Fix: Do Not Suppress Lambda Application Logs

Lambda already forwards application logs to CloudWatch Logs without any `loggingConfig` block, so
there is nothing to switch on. A violation means the function has *opted into* a log-level filter
that discards logs the control requires.

Either remove `applicationLogLevel` (all application logs are then forwarded), or raise it to a
level at least as verbose as the configured minimum (`TRACE` > `DEBUG` > `INFO` > `WARN` > `ERROR` > `FATAL`,
most verbose first). An adequate level is what gives output data validation and troubleshooting
sufficient detail:

```typescript
const myFunction = new aws.lambda.Function("my-function", {
    runtime: "nodejs20.x",
    handler: "index.handler",
    role: lambdaRole.arn,
    code: new pulumi.asset.AssetArchive({
        ".": new pulumi.asset.FileArchive("./app"),
    }),
    loggingConfig: {
        logFormat: "JSON",
        applicationLogLevel: "INFO", // not "ERROR"/"FATAL", which discard INFO and below
    },
});
```

