## Fix: Configure SSL/TLS Encryption for Aurora Cluster Instance

Aurora enforces TLS through the **DB cluster parameter group** attached to the cluster, not
through a flag on the instance. The parameter name differs by engine family:
`require_secure_transport` for MySQL-compatible engines, `rds.force_ssl` for
PostgreSQL-compatible engines.

```typescript
const clusterParamGroup = new aws.rds.ClusterParameterGroup("cluster-params", {
    family: "aurora-postgresql14",
    parameters: [
        {
            name: "rds.force_ssl",
            value: "1", // Enforce SSL/TLS for all connections
        },
    ],
});

const cluster = new aws.rds.Cluster("my-cluster", {
    engine: "aurora-postgresql",
    dbClusterParameterGroupName: clusterParamGroup.name, // Applies to every instance
    // ...
});

const clusterInstance = new aws.rds.ClusterInstance("my-cluster-instance", {
